      "sourceId": "xvfc-2020-21-report",
      "notes": "The Fifteenth Finance Commission issued two awards, and this is the first: a single-year report for 2020-21, separate from the 2021-26 report the other years use. Its horizontal shares are its own and differ from the later award's in every state — Andhra Pradesh 4.111 against 4.047, for instance. The vertical share is 41 per cent, which the Commission arrived at by holding the Fourteenth Commission's 42 per cent and cutting one percentage point because the reorganisation of Jammu and Kashmir moved an estimated 0.85 per cent of the pool to a union territory (para 1.17). This is why 2020-21 is not a Fourteenth Finance Commission year: that award ended with 2019-20, and 42 per cent appears here only as the level being adjusted.",
